# Tense TPM-04SH.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Tense TPM-04SH Energy Analyser — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: "Modbus Register TPM-04 SH SH-DL.pdf" (Basic Data Modbus Address).
# | Shared map for the Tense TPM-04 / TPM-04SH / TPM-01ES / TPM-01ESH family.
# | - Holding registers (FC03). Addresses are the raw register addresses in
# | decimal: 4000 = 0x0FA0 … 4419 = 0x1143 (manual's Dec and Hex are equal).
# | `area` defaults to "holding"; `word_order` defaults to "be" (manual lists
# | wide values most-significant word first: H/L and H3/H2/H1/L). Both omitted.
# | - "RESERVED read as 0" rows from the manual are intentionally not mapped.
# | - `scale` bakes in the device's fixed multiplier only.
# | 
# | CT/VT CAVEAT applies ONLY to the 16-bit voltage and current registers:
# | voltage(16-bit) = raw × VT × 0.1     current(16-bit) = raw × CT × 0.001
# | This map assumes a DIRECT connection (CT = 1, VT = 1). With external
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Tense
@model=TPM-04SH
@description=3-phase power-quality analyser (TPM-04 family) — V/I/P/Q/S with min/max/avg/demand, 64-bit energy, per-harmonic THD (3rd–31st), relay control.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/tense-tpm-04sh.toml; Source: "Modbus Register TPM-04 SH SH-DL.pdf" (Basic Data Modbus Address).. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
